1
00:00:02,509 --> 00:00:03,635
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:04,844 --> 00:00:06,596
Earth...

3
00:00:06,721 --> 00:00:08,723
Fire...

4
00:00:08,848 --> 00:00:11,267
Air.

5
00:00:11,351 --> 00:00:12,519
Long ago...

6
00:00:12,602 --> 00:00:15,355
The four nations lived
together in harmony.

7
00:00:15,438 --> 00:00:19,234
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

8
00:00:19,317 --> 00:00:23,696
Only the Avatar master of
all four elements could stop them.

9
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:25,490
But when the world
needed him most

10
00:00:25,573 --> 00:00:27,367
he vanished.

11
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:31,037
100 years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar

12
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,956
an airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:33,039 --> 00:00:35,166
And although his airbending
skills were great

14
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:37,794
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

15
00:00:37,877 --> 00:00:38,962
AANG: Oof.

16
00:00:39,045 --> 00:00:42,507
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

17
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:44,592
( ♪... )

18
00:00:47,929 --> 00:00:50,807
( MAN READING )

19
00:00:50,932 --> 00:00:52,892
AANG: Blending in is better
than hiding out.

20
00:00:53,017 --> 00:00:54,852
If we get Fire Nation disguises,

21
00:00:54,936 --> 00:00:57,647
we'll be just as safe as we would be
hiding in a cave.

22
00:00:57,730 --> 00:00:59,983
You have no right
to judge me, Uncle.

23
00:01:00,066 --> 00:01:04,237
I did what I had to do in Ba Sing Se,
and you were a fool for not joining me.

24
00:01:07,282 --> 00:01:10,076
I see you favor
the White Lotus Gambit.

25
00:01:10,159 --> 00:01:12,579
Not many still cling
to the ancient ways.

26
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:16,791
Those who do can always
find a friend.

27
00:01:26,050 --> 00:01:29,637
KATARA: Wow, this is amazing
to watch.

28
00:01:29,762 --> 00:01:32,515
Kind of makes you realize
how insignificant we are.

29
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:36,728
Eh, you've seen nothing once,
you've seen it 1,000 times.

30
00:01:36,811 --> 00:01:38,396
( ALL GASPING )

31
00:01:38,521 --> 00:01:39,731
SOKKA: Oh, man.

32
00:01:39,856 --> 00:01:41,566
You've never not seen
anything like this.

33
00:01:47,113 --> 00:01:48,364
( EXPLOSION )

34
00:01:57,206 --> 00:01:59,584
KATARA: The fire is gonna
destroy that town.

35
00:01:59,667 --> 00:02:01,044
AANG: Not if we can stop it.

36
00:02:01,544 --> 00:02:03,880
( GROWLING )

37
00:02:04,255 --> 00:02:05,590
There's a creek over here.

38
00:02:05,673 --> 00:02:07,425
I'll bend the water
on to the fire.

39
00:02:07,508 --> 00:02:10,303
Toph, let's make a trench
to keep the fire from coming any closer.

40
00:02:12,138 --> 00:02:13,181
What should I do?

41
00:02:13,306 --> 00:02:14,307
( MOMO SQUAWKING )

42
00:02:14,432 --> 00:02:15,933
Keep an eye on Momo.

43
00:02:16,726 --> 00:02:19,479
So what, I'm just
a lemur-sitter?

44
00:02:19,562 --> 00:02:20,563
There, there.

45
00:02:20,647 --> 00:02:21,648
Feel better?

46
00:02:30,281 --> 00:02:35,161
( GASPING )

47
00:02:58,434 --> 00:03:00,978
Sokka, stand clear.

48
00:03:01,062 --> 00:03:02,897
Right, stand clear.

49
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:04,148
Got it.

50
00:03:04,232 --> 00:03:05,733
( INHALING )

51
00:03:07,485 --> 00:03:09,612
( GASPING )

52
00:03:13,741 --> 00:03:16,035
Good work, everybody.

53
00:03:18,204 --> 00:03:20,456
( MOMO WARBLING )

54
00:03:32,218 --> 00:03:33,302
( GASPING )

55
00:03:33,386 --> 00:03:34,679
( MAKING EATING NOISES )

56
00:03:34,762 --> 00:03:36,097
MAN: Look at you.

57
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:38,766
You're just a fat,
disgusting old man.

58
00:03:39,350 --> 00:03:40,768
You do nothing, you say nothing.

59
00:03:40,893 --> 00:03:44,397
You just eat and roll around
in your own filth like a pig.

60
00:03:45,189 --> 00:03:46,357
You're a disgrace.

61
00:04:01,831 --> 00:04:05,501
These people have no idea how close
they were to getting toasted last night.

62
00:04:05,626 --> 00:04:08,504
Yeah, the worst thing
about being in disguise

63
00:04:08,588 --> 00:04:10,214
is we don't get
the hero worship anymore.

64
00:04:10,339 --> 00:04:12,091
I miss the love.

65
00:04:12,216 --> 00:04:14,969
Boo-hoo, poor heroes.

66
00:04:15,595 --> 00:04:16,971
What's your problem?

67
00:04:17,054 --> 00:04:19,265
You haven't even touched
your smoked sea slug.

68
00:04:19,348 --> 00:04:22,393
It's just, all you guys can do
this awesome bending stuff

69
00:04:22,477 --> 00:04:27,023
like putting out forest fires, and flying
around, and making other stuff fly around.

70
00:04:27,732 --> 00:04:29,484
I can't fly around, OK?

71
00:04:29,776 --> 00:04:32,153
I can't do anything.

72
00:04:32,487 --> 00:04:33,488
That's not true.

73
00:04:33,613 --> 00:04:35,948
No one can read a map like you.

74
00:04:36,032 --> 00:04:37,742
I can't read at all.

75
00:04:37,867 --> 00:04:40,495
Yeah, and who keeps us laughing
with sarcastic comments all the time?

76
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:43,456
I mean,
look at Katara's hair, right?

77
00:04:43,581 --> 00:04:45,500
- What's up with that?
- What?

78
00:04:45,625 --> 00:04:46,918
What's wrong with my hair?

79
00:04:47,043 --> 00:04:48,920
Nothing, I was just trying to...

80
00:04:49,045 --> 00:04:51,964
SOKKA: Look, I appreciate
the effort, but the fact is

81
00:04:52,089 --> 00:04:56,803
each of you is so amazing
and so special, and I'm not.

82
00:04:58,387 --> 00:05:00,681
I'm just the guy
in the group who's regular.

83
00:05:04,018 --> 00:05:05,561
I'm sorry you're feeling so down,

84
00:05:05,645 --> 00:05:08,189
but I hope you know none of us
see you that way.

85
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:13,152
I know something that's gonna
make you feel better.

86
00:05:13,236 --> 00:05:14,737
You do?

87
00:05:14,821 --> 00:05:16,781
Shopping.

88
00:05:17,824 --> 00:05:21,369
Maybe a little something
to reinvigorate my battling.

89
00:05:21,452 --> 00:05:22,578
Hey, how about these?

90
00:05:23,746 --> 00:05:24,872
Hi-ya!

91
00:05:24,997 --> 00:05:26,290
"Smack-a-dacka-doo!"

92
00:05:26,415 --> 00:05:30,294
( GRUNTING )

93
00:05:30,837 --> 00:05:32,255
AANG: What do you think?

94
00:05:34,215 --> 00:05:36,217
Pretty slick, huh?

95
00:05:36,342 --> 00:05:38,386
All I need to complete
the outfit is a wind sword.

96
00:05:38,511 --> 00:05:39,762
What's a wind sword?

97
00:05:39,887 --> 00:05:41,681
It's where I get a sword handle

98
00:05:41,806 --> 00:05:44,559
And then I just swing
this around and bend air out like a blade.

99
00:05:44,684 --> 00:05:47,728
( MAKING WHOOSHING SOUND )

100
00:05:47,854 --> 00:05:50,106
Yeah, nice.

101
00:05:50,231 --> 00:05:52,733
( WHIMPERING )

102
00:05:52,859 --> 00:05:54,360
I'll just stick to what I got.

103
00:05:59,574 --> 00:06:03,160
( GROANING )

104
00:06:03,286 --> 00:06:04,328
( GRUNTING )

105
00:06:19,343 --> 00:06:21,095
Ooh.

106
00:06:22,054 --> 00:06:24,181
That's what Sokka's
talking about.

107
00:06:24,265 --> 00:06:25,349
MAN: You have a good eye.

108
00:06:25,433 --> 00:06:27,226
That's an original from Piandao

109
00:06:27,310 --> 00:06:30,229
the greatest sword master
and sword maker in Fire Nation history.

110
00:06:30,354 --> 00:06:32,940
He lives in the big castle
up the road from here.

111
00:06:33,941 --> 00:06:35,401
That's it.

112
00:06:35,484 --> 00:06:36,986
That's what you needed
all along, Sokka.

113
00:06:37,069 --> 00:06:38,070
A sword?

114
00:06:38,154 --> 00:06:39,238
Not the sword.

115
00:06:39,322 --> 00:06:40,823
A master.

116
00:06:40,907 --> 00:06:42,950
We've all had masters
to help us get better.

117
00:06:43,117 --> 00:06:44,994
You should see if you
can study with Piandao.

118
00:06:45,077 --> 00:06:46,287
That's a great idea.

119
00:06:46,370 --> 00:06:49,165
I could've never gotten to where
I am without Master Pakku.

120
00:06:49,248 --> 00:06:50,750
Everyone needs a teacher.

121
00:06:51,334 --> 00:06:53,085
I learned from badger moles.

122
00:06:53,169 --> 00:06:55,171
They don't talk,
but they're still good teachers.

123
00:06:56,255 --> 00:06:59,216
It would be nice to be
a master swordfighter.

124
00:07:00,217 --> 00:07:01,802
All right, I'll talk to him.

125
00:07:09,435 --> 00:07:13,105
( GRUNTING )

126
00:07:26,452 --> 00:07:27,536
( GASPING )

127
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:28,955
Can I help you?

128
00:07:30,831 --> 00:07:32,375
I've come to train
with the master.

129
00:07:32,583 --> 00:07:36,253
You should know the master
turns almost everyone away.

130
00:07:36,337 --> 00:07:38,172
What did you bring him
to prove your worth?

131
00:07:39,215 --> 00:07:41,717
Well, uh...

132
00:07:41,801 --> 00:07:43,177
Right.

133
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:44,887
Let's get this over with.

134
00:07:55,898 --> 00:07:57,900
Master, my name is Sokka,

135
00:07:57,984 --> 00:08:00,319
and I wish to be instructed
in the way of the sword.

136
00:08:00,403 --> 00:08:01,612
PIANDAO: Sokka.

137
00:08:01,737 --> 00:08:03,406
That's an unusual name.

138
00:08:03,531 --> 00:08:05,032
Oh, uh, really?

139
00:08:05,157 --> 00:08:07,326
Uh, where I come from,
the Fire Nation colonies

140
00:08:07,410 --> 00:08:11,163
it's a pretty normal name,
for Fire Nation colonials.

141
00:08:11,247 --> 00:08:12,915
PIANDAO: Let me guess.

142
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:15,543
You've come hundreds of miles
from your little village

143
00:08:15,668 --> 00:08:18,462
where you're the best
swordsman in town

144
00:08:18,546 --> 00:08:21,674
and you think you deserve
to learn from the master.

145
00:08:21,799 --> 00:08:24,260
Well, actually, I've been
all over the world.

146
00:08:24,593 --> 00:08:26,887
PIANDAO: Yep, here we go.

147
00:08:26,971 --> 00:08:30,933
And I know one thing for sure,
I have a lot to learn.

148
00:08:31,851 --> 00:08:34,979
You're not doing a very good job
of selling yourself.

149
00:08:35,062 --> 00:08:36,564
I know.

150
00:08:36,647 --> 00:08:39,483
Your butler told me that when I met you,
I would have to prove my worth

151
00:08:39,567 --> 00:08:42,361
But the truth is,
I don't know if I am worthy.

152
00:08:42,445 --> 00:08:44,739
Hm, I see.

153
00:08:45,698 --> 00:08:50,494
Well, then, let's find out
together how worthy you are.

154
00:08:52,580 --> 00:08:54,373
I will train you.

155
00:09:00,463 --> 00:09:04,800
The first thing you must learn is that
your weapon is an extension of yourself.

156
00:09:04,884 --> 00:09:08,137
You must think of it as
another part of your own body.

157
00:09:10,014 --> 00:09:11,390
Like a second head.

158
00:09:11,766 --> 00:09:16,520
Well, more like
an extra-long, really sharp arm.

159
00:09:16,604 --> 00:09:20,566
The sword is a simple tool,
but in the hands of a master

160
00:09:20,649 --> 00:09:26,363
it becomes the most versatile of weapons,
and just as the imagination is limitless

161
00:09:26,447 --> 00:09:29,700
so too are the possibilities
of the sword.

162
00:09:32,369 --> 00:09:33,704
AANG: What should we do today?

163
00:09:33,788 --> 00:09:34,997
I'm tapped out.

164
00:09:35,081 --> 00:09:36,999
I already picked my toes, twice.

165
00:09:37,083 --> 00:09:38,584
Twice?

166
00:09:38,667 --> 00:09:40,044
The first time was for cleaning,

167
00:09:40,127 --> 00:09:43,547
but the second time's just for
the sweet picking sensation.

168
00:09:44,090 --> 00:09:45,674
Sokka's been in charge
of the schedule.

169
00:09:45,758 --> 00:09:47,676
I'm not sure
what we should be doing.

170
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:50,930
Plus, it's so hot today.

171
00:09:51,013 --> 00:09:52,306
How hot is it?

172
00:09:52,389 --> 00:09:53,390
I don't know.

173
00:09:53,474 --> 00:09:54,725
Real hot?

174
00:09:54,850 --> 00:10:00,898
It's so hot, it's so hot,
Momo is shedding like Appa.

175
00:10:00,981 --> 00:10:04,568
Huh, huh?

176
00:10:05,569 --> 00:10:07,571
I guess the jokes
don't run in the family.

177
00:10:07,863 --> 00:10:09,865
KATARA: Oh, everyone's a critic.

178
00:10:09,949 --> 00:10:11,408
( APPA GROWLING )

179
00:10:11,492 --> 00:10:13,869
( GRUNTING )

180
00:10:21,627 --> 00:10:26,841
The warrior practices a variety
of arts to keep his mind sharp and fluid.

181
00:10:26,924 --> 00:10:29,760
The first you will learn
is calligraphy.

182
00:10:29,844 --> 00:10:31,428
Write your name.

183
00:10:31,929 --> 00:10:34,473
Writing my name will make me
a better swordsman?

184
00:10:34,598 --> 00:10:38,853
When you write your name,
you stamp the paper with your identity.

185
00:10:38,936 --> 00:10:43,232
You must learn to use your sword
to stamp your identity on a battlefield.

186
00:10:47,361 --> 00:10:53,200
Remember, you cannot take back a stroke of
the brush, or a stroke of the sword.

187
00:10:57,329 --> 00:10:59,498
You are getting ink
on your face.

188
00:10:59,582 --> 00:11:01,041
I am?

189
00:11:01,125 --> 00:11:02,376
I am.

190
00:11:02,501 --> 00:11:04,837
So this is about putting
my identity on the page, right?

191
00:11:21,979 --> 00:11:27,610
( GRUNTING )

192
00:11:30,487 --> 00:11:34,950
Landscape painting teaches a warrior
to hold the lay of the land in his mind.

193
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:38,495
( GRUNTING )

194
00:11:38,579 --> 00:11:41,957
In battle, you only have an instant
to take everything in.

195
00:11:50,007 --> 00:11:52,635
Now, paint it.

196
00:11:53,761 --> 00:11:54,887
And no peeking.

197
00:12:09,693 --> 00:12:12,071
SOKKA: I'm finished.

198
00:12:14,031 --> 00:12:15,616
You added a rainbow.

199
00:12:16,825 --> 00:12:18,452
Is that OK?

200
00:12:18,577 --> 00:12:20,537
( SIGHING )

201
00:12:23,499 --> 00:12:25,251
( GRUNTING )

202
00:12:25,376 --> 00:12:27,294
PIANDAO: Sokka.

203
00:12:27,419 --> 00:12:29,213
( GRUNTING )

204
00:12:29,338 --> 00:12:31,465
Concentrate on
what you're doing.

205
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:36,887
Rock gardening teaches the warrior
to manipulate his surroundings

206
00:12:37,012 --> 00:12:39,515
and use them to his advantage.

207
00:12:40,057 --> 00:12:43,936
Hm, manipulate them
to my advantage.

208
00:12:44,019 --> 00:12:45,187
Oh.

209
00:12:47,564 --> 00:12:49,900
( GRUNTING )

210
00:13:00,661 --> 00:13:03,205
Ah.

211
00:13:04,581 --> 00:13:06,292
( GASPING )

212
00:13:06,375 --> 00:13:08,585
Hey, would you mind grabbing
a cold drink for me?

213
00:13:08,752 --> 00:13:09,753
( GASPING )

214
00:13:09,837 --> 00:13:11,755
I'll take a slice of lemon
in mine, please.

215
00:13:11,839 --> 00:13:13,090
( SIGHING )

216
00:13:50,711 --> 00:13:52,171
What's going on in there?

217
00:13:57,843 --> 00:13:59,053
Crazy old man.

218
00:14:05,809 --> 00:14:07,603
KATARA: So where are
we going next?

219
00:14:08,103 --> 00:14:09,730
We're starting from here.

220
00:14:09,813 --> 00:14:11,565
No, we're over on this island.

221
00:14:11,982 --> 00:14:14,735
You noodle-brains don't know
what you're doing.

222
00:14:14,860 --> 00:14:16,612
I miss Sokka.

223
00:14:16,695 --> 00:14:18,489
Ooh, I got one.

224
00:14:18,614 --> 00:14:22,242
If you miss him so much,
why don't you marry him?

225
00:14:29,750 --> 00:14:31,835
PIANDAO: You've had a good
first day of training.

226
00:14:31,919 --> 00:14:33,504
I have?

227
00:14:33,629 --> 00:14:35,964
But I thought I messed up
every single thing we worked on.

228
00:14:36,048 --> 00:14:39,301
You messed things up
in a very special way.

229
00:14:39,426 --> 00:14:42,096
You are ready for a real sword.

230
00:14:42,179 --> 00:14:43,180
( GASPING )

231
00:14:43,263 --> 00:14:44,306
Are you giving me one of yours?

232
00:14:44,431 --> 00:14:45,432
No.

233
00:14:45,516 --> 00:14:46,600
( GROANING )

234
00:14:46,725 --> 00:14:49,853
Your sword must be
an extension of yourself

235
00:14:49,978 --> 00:14:53,899
So tomorrow, you will make
your own sword.

236
00:15:02,199 --> 00:15:06,703
Choosing the correct material is the
most important step in crafting a sword.

237
00:15:06,787 --> 00:15:09,164
You must trust your steel
with your life.

238
00:15:09,248 --> 00:15:10,249
Choose carefully.

239
00:15:13,377 --> 00:15:15,671
( GRUNTING )

240
00:15:17,339 --> 00:15:19,174
Master, would it be possible for me to

241
00:15:19,258 --> 00:15:22,010
leave and bring back
a special material for my sword?

242
00:15:22,094 --> 00:15:24,346
I wouldn't have it
any other way.

243
00:15:27,641 --> 00:15:29,601
- Sokka's coming.
-( GASPING )

244
00:15:29,685 --> 00:15:31,145
Hey, guys.
What are you doing?

245
00:15:31,228 --> 00:15:32,646
AANG: Sokka?
TOPH: You're back.

246
00:15:32,729 --> 00:15:34,440
We missed you so much.

247
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:36,358
Say something funny.

248
00:15:36,442 --> 00:15:37,901
Funny how?

249
00:15:37,985 --> 00:15:40,154
( LAUGHING )

250
00:15:40,779 --> 00:15:41,989
What's their deal?

251
00:15:42,114 --> 00:15:43,323
I don't know.

252
00:15:43,449 --> 00:15:45,075
They missed you or something.

253
00:15:45,159 --> 00:15:46,743
I didn't care.

254
00:15:46,827 --> 00:15:49,204
Thanks.
That warms my heart.

255
00:15:49,329 --> 00:15:50,706
Anyway, I need some help.

256
00:16:05,679 --> 00:16:07,890
( BREATHING HEAVILY )

257
00:16:26,825 --> 00:16:27,868
Who's this?

258
00:16:27,951 --> 00:16:29,786
Oh, these are my friends.

259
00:16:29,870 --> 00:16:31,872
Just other good
Fire Nation folks.

260
00:16:33,081 --> 00:16:35,751
Do you think we can make
a sword out of a meteorite?

261
00:16:36,543 --> 00:16:40,172
We'll make a sword unlike
any other in the world.

262
00:17:38,230 --> 00:17:42,401
Sokka, when you first arrived,
you were so unsure.

263
00:17:42,484 --> 00:17:45,195
You even seemed
down on yourself.

264
00:17:45,279 --> 00:17:47,864
But I saw something
in you right away.

265
00:17:47,990 --> 00:17:52,661
I saw a heart as strong as
a lion turtle, and twice as big

266
00:17:52,744 --> 00:17:56,999
and as we trained, it wasn't
your skills that impressed me.

267
00:17:57,082 --> 00:18:00,711
No, it certainly
wasn't your skills.

268
00:18:01,962 --> 00:18:05,132
You showed something
beyond that.

269
00:18:05,841 --> 00:18:10,095
Creativity, versatility,
intelligence.

270
00:18:10,178 --> 00:18:13,599
These are the traits
that define a great swordsman

271
00:18:13,682 --> 00:18:17,436
and these are the traits
that define you.

272
00:18:17,519 --> 00:18:21,732
You told me you didn't know
if you were worthy

273
00:18:21,857 --> 00:18:27,738
but I believe that you are more worthy
than any man I have ever trained.

274
00:18:30,782 --> 00:18:32,367
I'm sorry, master.

275
00:18:32,451 --> 00:18:33,493
You're wrong.

276
00:18:33,619 --> 00:18:35,829
I am not worthy.

277
00:18:36,038 --> 00:18:37,664
I'm not who you think I am.

278
00:18:37,789 --> 00:18:38,874
I'm not from the Fire Nation.

279
00:18:38,999 --> 00:18:41,293
I'm from the Southern
Water Tribe.

280
00:18:41,376 --> 00:18:44,046
I lied so that I could
learn swordsmanship from you.

281
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:45,964
I'm sorry.

282
00:18:47,257 --> 00:18:49,426
I'm sorry, too.

283
00:18:49,509 --> 00:18:51,219
( GASPING )

284
00:18:52,596 --> 00:18:56,642
No, this is my fight, alone.

285
00:19:00,604 --> 00:19:03,357
You used to be
the pride of the Fire Nation.

286
00:19:03,482 --> 00:19:06,234
Our top general,
The Dragon of the West.

287
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:10,072
Now, look at you.

288
00:19:10,822 --> 00:19:12,115
Look what you've become.

289
00:19:23,835 --> 00:19:24,920
( GRUNTING )

290
00:19:48,735 --> 00:19:51,822
( GRUNTING )

291
00:20:05,377 --> 00:20:07,212
PIANDAO: Excellent.

292
00:20:07,295 --> 00:20:09,297
Using your superior agility
against an older opponent.

293
00:20:09,423 --> 00:20:10,632
Smart.

294
00:20:15,595 --> 00:20:17,305
( GRUNTING )

295
00:20:27,774 --> 00:20:29,151
PIANDAO: Good use of terrain.

296
00:20:29,234 --> 00:20:30,402
Fighting from the high ground.

297
00:20:35,866 --> 00:20:37,159
( GRUNTING )

298
00:20:56,052 --> 00:20:58,638
Yes, use your surroundings.

299
00:20:58,764 --> 00:21:00,515
Make them fight for you.

300
00:21:01,892 --> 00:21:03,393
( SCREAMING )

301
00:21:03,477 --> 00:21:05,437
( PANTING )

302
00:21:10,692 --> 00:21:11,735
( GRUNTING )

303
00:21:15,113 --> 00:21:16,573
( COUGHING )

304
00:21:17,783 --> 00:21:19,743
Very resourceful.

305
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:50,023
Excellent work, Sokka.

306
00:21:58,198 --> 00:22:01,576
I think I'm a little old
to be fighting the Avatar.

307
00:22:03,161 --> 00:22:04,454
How did you know?

308
00:22:04,621 --> 00:22:06,289
Oh, I've been around a while.

309
00:22:06,414 --> 00:22:08,166
You pick things up.

310
00:22:08,291 --> 00:22:10,836
Of course, I knew from the beginning
that Sokka was Water Tribe.

311
00:22:11,670 --> 00:22:15,215
You might want to think of
a better Fire Nation cover name.

312
00:22:15,298 --> 00:22:16,508
Try "Lee."

313
00:22:16,633 --> 00:22:18,760
There's a million Lees.

314
00:22:18,844 --> 00:22:22,013
But why would you agree
to train someone from the water tribe?

315
00:22:22,097 --> 00:22:25,225
The way of the sword doesn't
belong to any one nation.

316
00:22:25,308 --> 00:22:28,061
Knowledge of the arts
belongs to us all.

317
00:22:31,439 --> 00:22:36,778
Sokka, you must continue
your training on your own.

318
00:22:36,945 --> 00:22:40,740
If you stay on this path,
I know that one day

319
00:22:40,824 --> 00:22:43,827
you will become an even
greater master than I am.

320
00:22:52,586 --> 00:22:54,588
Wait.

321
00:22:55,130 --> 00:22:59,634
The master wanted you to have this,
as something to remember him by.

322
00:23:06,391 --> 00:23:07,934
It's a Pai Sho tile.

323
00:23:08,018 --> 00:23:09,936
AANG: The White Lotus.
Hm.

324
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:11,313
KATARA: What does it mean?

325
00:23:11,396 --> 00:23:12,856
I have no idea.

326
00:23:16,234 --> 00:23:17,861
Ooh, that reminds me.

327
00:23:17,944 --> 00:23:19,487
Toph, I thought
you might like this

328
00:23:19,571 --> 00:23:22,240
Since you've probably never had a chance
to bend space earth before.

329
00:23:23,074 --> 00:23:24,242
Sweet.

330
00:23:26,411 --> 00:23:27,704
Check this out.

331
00:23:30,373 --> 00:23:32,751
You know, I don't think there's
such a thing as "space earth."

332
00:23:32,834 --> 00:23:35,712
If it's from space,
then it's not really earth.

333
00:23:35,795 --> 00:23:37,547
SOKKA: Must you ruin everything?

334
00:23:37,631 --> 00:23:39,716
KATARA: I can't believe
I missed you.

335
00:23:46,932 --> 00:23:50,352
( ♪... )
